<title>USA: Amgen patent upheld by US Appeals Court.</title>
<headline>Amgen patent upheld by US Appeals Court.</headline>
<dateline>THOUSAND OAKS, Calif. 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pharmaceutical powerhouse Amgen Inc said a U.S. appeals court upheld a lower court ruling affirming its patent for Epogen against claims by Genetics Institute Inc.</p>
<p>The ruling bans Genetics Institute from asserting a claim to Amgen's Epogen, a drug which stimulates red blood cell production and is widely used by kidney dialysis patients.  </p>
<p>The ruling is the latest development in a 10-year battle between Amgen and Genetics Institute.</p>
<p>Worldwide sales of Epogen last year totaled $883 million.</p>
</text>
